  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the operator, I want to keep today's topic rows (the unread dot and the flag icons in front of the title) as an **experimental option**, while the default rows follow ezzz's legacy layout of #817 (the whole row tinted by flag type, no icon before the title). (Operator, 2026-11-14.)\n\n### Where it lives\n\n- Behind `ExperimentalFeature.flagIconRows` (Réglages › Expérimental › « Lignes avec icônes de drapeau »), set up by #903.\n- Code: today's row markers (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicRowView.swift:74-80`: blue unread dot, yellow star, blue and red flags) move to `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/FlagIconRows/` in #903. The place where #817's tint replaces them carries `// EXPERIMENTAL(flagIconRows, #905)`.\n- **Order:** #903 moves the current view first, then #817 builds the legacy default next to it. #817 must not delete the current markers.\n\n### What the option shows\n\n- Switch **on**: today's rows (dot and flag icons before the title), plus the #808 pills where they apply.\n- Switch **off** (default): #817 (legacy row tint `rowBackgroundTint(for:)` @ `87fe0d1c` `MainWindow.swift:477-491`, super favourites tint `Favorites.swift:1134`, inset card with grey side margins, page count and « last poster – date »).\n\n### Rules\n\n- Claimed by the operator (`human/francoisgn`). M5. Agents touch it only on the operator's go.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Both row styles render from the same row model. A hosted test covers each style.\n- [ ] Switching the option redraws the lists without a reload.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
